<section class="gg-mimc-manager gg-mimc-config">
  <header class="gg-mimc-hero"><div><div class="gg-mimc-eyebrow">GREENE GAMING · PORTABLE CONFIGURATION</div><h1>Configuration Import / Export</h1><p>Prepare in a local world, transfer to Forge, preserve private evidence.</p></div></header>
  <aside class="gg-mimc-notice">Private files may contain spoilers, GM notes and licensed adventure material. Never commit your campaign JSON or custom assets to a public repository. This is not a full world backup. Only module-managed data is transferred.</aside>
  <section class="gg-mimc-cue-group gg-mimc-evidence-fields">
    <h2>Export configuration</h2>
    <label>Export mode<select name="mode">{{#each modes}}<option value="{{id}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{name}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label>
    <p>Setup: scenes, cast, lighting, case subject and chase requirements. Preparation: also private evidence drafts and court journal text/art references. Campaign state: also published snapshots, placements, exhibits and chase progress.</p>
    <div class="gg-mimc-config-checks">{{#each features}}<label><input type="checkbox" data-feature="{{id}}" {{#if selected}}checked{{/if}}> {{title}}</label>{{/each}}
    <label><input type="checkbox" name="macros" {{#if macros}}checked{{/if}}> Include installed standard GM shortcuts</label></div>
    <div class="gg-mimc-actions"><button type="button" data-action="export"><i class="fa-solid fa-download"></i> Generate private JSON</button><button type="button" data-action="exportZIP"><i class="fa-solid fa-file-zipper"></i> Generate private ZIP</button></div>
    <p data-export-status aria-live="polite">ZIP includes referenced custom PNG, JPEG and WebP images. Built-in module artwork remains a reference.</p>
    {{#if zipName}}<div class="gg-mimc-display-state"><strong>{{zipName}}</strong><p>{{zipCount}} custom images · {{zipSize}} MB</p></div>
    <div class="gg-mimc-actions"><button type="button" data-action="saveZIP"><i class="fa-solid fa-floppy-disk"></i> Save ZIP</button>{{#if canCopyZIP}}<button type="button" data-action="copyZIP">Copy ZIP data (Windows fallback)</button>{{/if}}</div>
    <p>If Foundry desktop does not save the file, open the same world in a browser and generate/save the ZIP there.</p>
    {{#if canCopyZIP}}<details><summary>Windows desktop clipboard fallback</summary><p>Copy the command below into PowerShell first (do not execute yet). Return here and click Copy ZIP data, then run the command in PowerShell without copying anything else. It saves the ZIP to your Desktop, replacing a file of the same name. Keep the clipboard contents private.</p><textarea rows="3" readonly spellcheck="false">{{zipCommand}}</textarea></details>{{/if}}{{/if}}
    {{#if exportName}}<div class="gg-mimc-display-state"><strong>{{exportName}}</strong><p>Save to a location you choose if supported, or copy the JSON into Notepad and save as this filename. Foundry desktop may not support browser downloads.</p></div>
    <div class="gg-mimc-actions"><button type="button" data-action="saveFile"><i class="fa-solid fa-floppy-disk"></i> Save file</button><button type="button" data-action="copyJSON"><i class="fa-solid fa-copy"></i> Copy JSON</button><button type="button" data-action="selectJSON">Select all JSON</button></div>
    <label>Private configuration output<textarea name="exportText" rows="7" readonly spellcheck="false">{{exportText}}</textarea></label>{{/if}}
  </section>
  <section class="gg-mimc-cue-group gg-mimc-evidence-fields">
    <h2>Import configuration</h2>
    <label>Configuration JSON or preparation ZIP<input type="file" accept=".json,.zip,application/json,application/zip" name="file"></label>
    <label>Or paste configuration JSON<textarea name="pasted" rows="4" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Paste exported private JSON here"></textarea></label>
    <div class="gg-mimc-actions"><button type="button" data-action="loadPasted">Load pasted JSON</button></div>
    {{#if filename}}<p>Selected: <strong>{{filename}}</strong></p>{{/if}}
    {{#if packageCount}}<aside class="gg-mimc-notice">{{packageCount}} bundled images validated. They will be uploaded only when you apply the configuration. Uploaded files may be directly accessible by URL; keep asset links private.</aside>{{/if}}
    <label>Asset path replacements (JSON object; optional)<textarea name="mapping" rows="3">{{mapping}}</textarea></label>
    <p>For JSON imports, upload custom artwork to Forge first. ZIP imports can upload included images automatically. Map old paths to new paths if needed, e.g. {"worlds/local/art/npc.png":"your-forge-asset-path/npc.png"}. Included module assets retain their original paths.</p>
    <div class="gg-mimc-actions"><button type="button" data-action="preview">Validate &amp; preview</button></div>
    {{#if preview}}
    <div data-preview-status>Preview: {{preview.data.mode}} — {{preview.summary.scenes}} scenes, {{preview.summary.drafts}} drafts, {{preview.summary.published}} public snapshots, {{preview.summary.officials}} court journals, {{preview.summary.assets}} referenced assets.</div>
    {{#if preview.missing.length}}<aside class="gg-mimc-notice"><strong>Missing assets — import blocked</strong>{{#each preview.missing}}<p>{{path}}</p>{{/each}}</aside>{{else}}<p>External referenced images loaded successfully on this GM client. Bundled images will be checked after upload.</p>{{/if}}
    {{#if preview.conflicts.length}}<div><strong>Existing destination items</strong>{{#each preview.conflicts}}<p>{{this}}</p>{{/each}}</div>{{/if}}
    <div class="gg-mimc-config-checks">
      <label><input type="checkbox" name="replace" {{#if replace}}checked{{/if}}> Apply imported settings to existing managed items (otherwise merge missing only)</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" name="confirmReplace"> I understand managed settings and matching private journal content may be updated</label>
      {{#if campaign}}<label><input type="checkbox" name="progress" {{#if progress}}checked{{/if}}> Restore campaign progress, including making exported public snapshots player-readable</label>{{/if}}
      {{#if packageCount}}<label><input type="checkbox" name="confirmAssets"> I authorize upload of the included custom artwork to the destination asset library</label>{{/if}}
      <label><input type="checkbox" name="confirm"> I have backed up this world, reviewed the preview and understand import is not transactional</label>
    </div>
    <div class="gg-mimc-actions"><button type="button" data-action="apply" {{#unless canApply}}disabled{{/unless}}><i class="fa-solid fa-file-import"></i> Apply configuration</button></div>
    {{/if}}
    {{#if log.length}}<h3>Import results</h3>{{#each log}}<p>{{this}}</p>{{/each}}{{/if}}
  </section>
</section>
